WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
When the hot summer rolled in, spirits were high as a new season was upon us.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.820
With the abundance of variety we got in the spring season and Re:Zero grabbing the entire community,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.160
we were all hoping that the hype train would continue

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.700
and just as that thought past our minds we were stop dead in our tracks

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.540
in a series that started a long time ago in a manga far far delayed...

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.660
The epic saga continued

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:32.000
*Star Wars main theme playing*

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.720
It was an optimistic time to be a Berserk fan.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.260
8 years had passed and we finally we got off a fucking boat,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.920
and a new adaptation was announced

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.280
signaling the first time we could finally stop sucking off the Golden Age arc.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.920
Yet in this time of optimism, a shroud of dread loomed among the fandom...

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.180
OH GOD, WHAT DID YOU DO TO IT!

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:58.220
Yes 2016 was the year the Berserk franchise genuinely imploded by releasing one of the most

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.140
awful adaptations ever to grace such a beloved franchise

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.580
The majority of people were already pretty cautious

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.540
as soon as the term 'CG' was being thrown around in early trailers

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.120
but nothing could have prepared us for the disaster that would befall everyone

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.340
and here's the thing

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.900
It wasn't just the CG that ruined it

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.760
'Ajin' already proved earlier in the year

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.920
that dodgy CG can be saved by good writing which Berserk should have

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.280
but the adaptation failed in almost every front

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.880
to the point where it just felt like a high-budget fan project

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.860
made by people who had little to no knowledge of filmmaking

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.020
From terrible action direction, awful shot composition, confusing cuts,

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.340
amateur lighting, ugly color palettes, junky frame rates and hilarious sound designers

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.580
that transformed Guts' steel behemoth of a sword into a fucking frying pan...

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.020
*Frying Pan Hit Sound*

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.120
For Berserk fans it was like watching a car crash in slow motion

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.260
and the only real good things to come of it were the the opening and the hilarious fan reaction.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.140
Re:Zero may have been this years's show containing suffering,

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.140
but Berserk is a pure embodiment of it for characters and fandom alike

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:04.460
from Guts' journey to waiting for new chapters to just hoping for a single decent complete anime adaptation

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:09.300
so if you're thinking about getting into Berserk just read the manga cause here's the BERSERK 2016 experience

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:15.020
*Music*

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.340
Outside of the fiery heat of the Berserk fandom

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.700
the hottest new show of the summer was of course 'MobPsycho 100'

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.280
the spiritual successor to and from the same author as  'One Punch Man'

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.640
which we can totally tell because half of character designs look like

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.780
they just took Saitama and gave him a different wig,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.560
so of course we all prepared for this to essentially be 'One Psychic Boy'

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.740
but beyond the first few episodes it definitely differentiates itself from just being that:

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.640
The journey our timid protagonist makes to constantly better himself

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.800
drove the theme of self improvement throughout the show

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.800
complete with the likable supporting cast

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.900
like the Saul Goodman of anime Reagan,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.540
a charismatic con artist unmatched in his talent at selling bullshit

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.880
though if there is one stand out thing about this show

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.960
is one of the best showcases of absolutely breathtaking and unique animation

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:00.620
with some of the most magnificent looking scenes of the year, making it a must-watch for any animation fan.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.660
'Sweetness and Lightning' gave Japan's latest attempt at combating the country's declining birth rates

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.540
by parading around the advantages of having an adorable daughter in:

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.840
But the daughter would have to be pretty fucking sweet to convince Otakus to do that,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.480
so how sweet could they make her?

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.620
Aaaaand I have diabetes now.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.280
'91 Days' proved to the world that Japan are indeed capable of making a dark and gritty gangster drama,

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.440
without forcing in supernatural bullshit making the second half borderline unwatchable,

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:34.960
with the highly westernized historical story of revenge, featuring a very muted and (serbia) down to earth artstyle

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.220
this may actually be the least anime "anime" to have aired in 2016

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:44.080
and did this by very obviously but tastefully sucking off classic Hollywood gangster films.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.940
Fans of the ever popular shoujo manga 'Orange' were treated to an anime adaptation,

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.400
in the story of a girl who receives a letter from herself 10 years forward in time

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.720
in order to free herself from her regrets of her youth,

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.680
of the course the concept was always going to be a never ending feels train

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.040
as when is messing around with your past in fiction ever gone well!?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.440
But it does beg the question of:

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.480
if you could sent the message to yourself in the past that could literally change your life

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:06.640
What would it be?

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:16.080
*Sad Music*

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.880
'Tales of Zestiria the X' did what Ufotable does best

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.060
by presenting more stunning scenes of digital animation

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.180
while overall not being that impressive of a show,

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.760
when they aren't busy sucking off Type-Moon behind the scenes.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.920
For those who needed some serenity in their lives

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.100
'Amanchu!' was the perfect show for those who just needed something calming

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.000
*Demonic Voice*
{You must cleanse the world of this ignorant filth}

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.480
giving us one of the most atmospheric, peaceful

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.320
*Demonic Voice*
{BURN IT, BURN IT ALL DOWN!}

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.000
and tranquil slice of life anime to come out in the summer

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.160
